  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of Solar Tuk Tuk for Public Transportation for Rural in Gedaref State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In rural Gedaref State, Sudan, transportation for people and agricultural goods relies on outdated petrol-powered three-wheelers and donkey carts, which are inefficient, costly, and environmentally harmful. Rising fuel prices and unreliable petrol availability make it difficult for farmers to access markets, often rendering trade unprofitable and limiting local economic growth. These challenges constrain value chains, increase post-harvest losses, and deepen rural poverty while contributing to e</narrative>
  </description>
